Relevant columns and their possible usage for this task  
• "PatientID": patient identifier (identification detail)  
• "idc_case_id": IDC‑assigned patient / case UUID (identification detail)  
• "PatientSex": required = ‘M’ (sex filter)  
• "PatientAge": stored as text such as ‘018Y’ – extract / test numeric part = 18 (age filter)  
• "BodyPartExamined": must contain ‘MEDIASTINUM’ (anatomical filter)  
• "StudyInstanceUID": unique study identifier (study detail)  
• "StudyDate": study date column – must be > 2014‑09‑01 (date filter)  
• "StudyDescription": free‑text description of study (study detail)  
• "SeriesInstanceUID": unique series identifier (series detail)  
• "SeriesDescription": free‑text description of series (series detail)  
• "SeriesDate": creation date of the series (series detail)  
• "SeriesNumber": number that orders series within a study (series detail)  
• "InstanceNumber": image number inside a series (instance detail)  
• "instance_size": size in bytes of each DICOM object (needed for total size)  
• "gcs_url": full GCS path to each object (object‑level storage location)  
• "aws_url": full AWS path to each object (object‑level storage location)  
• "series_gcs_url": GCS folder that contains the whole series (series‑level location)  
• "series_aws_url": AWS folder that contains the whole series (series‑level location)  
• "collection_id": collection short id (high‑level identification)  
• "collection_name": collection name shown by TCIA (high‑level identification)

Typical conditions that may be used  
• "PatientSex" = 'M'  
• "PatientAge" ILIKE '018%'  (or = '018Y')  
• "BodyPartExamined" ILIKE '%MEDIASTINUM%'  
• "StudyDate" > '2014‑09‑01' (DATE literal)  

Ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries  
(Adjust limit rows as needed – here LIMIT 20.)

```sql
-- 1. Description: Inspect distinct values stored in BodyPartExamined to verify spelling / letter case variations
SELECT DISTINCT "BodyPartExamined"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Look at sample PatientAge strings for adult patients
SELECT DISTINCT "PatientAge"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "PatientAge" ILIKE '%Y'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Preview rows where BodyPartExamined mentions 'MEDIASTINUM' in any shape
SELECT "PatientID", "PatientSex", "PatientAge", "BodyPartExamined", "StudyDate"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "BodyPartExamined" ILIKE '%MEDIASTINUM%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Count distinct male patients whose age text starts with 018 and study after 2014‑09‑01
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT "PatientID") AS "male_18_patient_cnt"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "PatientSex" = 'M'
  AND "PatientAge" ILIKE '018%'
  AND "BodyPartExamined" ILIKE '%MEDIASTINUM%'
  AND "StudyDate" > '2014-09-01';
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Retrieve identification columns for qualifying patients/studies
SELECT DISTINCT
       "PatientID",
       "idc_case_id",
       "StudyInstanceUID",
       "StudyDate",
       "StudyDescription"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "PatientSex" = 'M'
  AND "PatientAge" ILIKE '018%'
  AND "BodyPartExamined" ILIKE '%MEDIASTINUM%'
  AND "StudyDate" > '2014-09-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: List series information for those studies (series uid, number, description, dates)
SELECT DISTINCT
       "SeriesInstanceUID",
       "SeriesNumber",
       "SeriesDate",
       "SeriesDescription",
       "StudyInstanceUID"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "PatientSex" = 'M'
  AND "PatientAge" ILIKE '018%'
  AND "BodyPartExamined" ILIKE '%MEDIASTINUM%'
  AND "StudyDate" > '2014-09-01'
ORDER BY "SeriesDate"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Retrieve storage folder locations (GCS & AWS) for each qualifying series
SELECT DISTINCT
       "SeriesInstanceUID",
       "series_gcs_url",
       "series_aws_url"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "PatientSex" = 'M'
  AND "PatientAge" ILIKE '018%'
  AND "BodyPartExamined" ILIKE '%MEDIASTINUM%'
  AND "StudyDate" > '2014-09-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Sample object‑level storage URLs together with instance size
SELECT
       "SeriesInstanceUID",
       "InstanceNumber",
       "gcs_url",
       "aws_url",
       "instance_size"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "PatientSex" = 'M'
  AND "PatientAge" ILIKE '018%'
  AND "BodyPartExamined" ILIKE '%MEDIASTINUM%'
  AND "StudyDate" > '2014-09-01'
ORDER BY "SeriesInstanceUID", CAST("InstanceNumber" AS INTEGER)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Aggregate total size (MB) per series for the selected cohort
SELECT
       "SeriesInstanceUID",
       ROUND(SUM("instance_size") / 1000000, 2) AS "series_size_mb",
       MIN("series_gcs_url") AS "series_gcs_url",
       MIN("series_aws_url") AS "series_aws_url"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "PatientSex" = 'M'
  AND "PatientAge" ILIKE '018%'
  AND "BodyPartExamined" ILIKE '%MEDIASTINUM%'
  AND "StudyDate" > '2014-09-01'
GROUP BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
ORDER BY "series_size_mb" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final combined view – patient, study, series, storage locations, total series size (MB)
SELECT
       "PatientID",
       "idc_case_id",
       "PatientSex",
       "PatientAge",
       "StudyInstanceUID",
       "StudyDate",
       "SeriesInstanceUID",
       ROUND(SUM("instance_size") / 1000000, 2) AS "series_size_mb",
       MIN("series_gcs_url") AS "series_gcs_url",
       MIN("series_aws_url") AS "series_aws_url"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "PatientSex" = 'M'
  AND "PatientAge" ILIKE '018%'
  AND "BodyPartExamined" ILIKE '%MEDIASTINUM%'
  AND "StudyDate" > '2014-09-01'
GROUP BY
       "PatientID",
       "idc_case_id",
       "PatientSex",
       "PatientAge",
       "StudyInstanceUID",
       "StudyDate",
       "SeriesInstanceUID"
ORDER BY "PatientID", "SeriesInstanceUID"
LIMIT 20;
```
